# DME101.030 — Ultrasonic Osteogenesis Stimulator Coverage (Stage 1: local-decision-support)
library "Ultrasonic Osteogenesis Stimulator Coverage".

/*
========================= NOT PROMOTABLE (proof-pending) =========================
This is the DECOMPOSED reference encoding. It expresses the policy's full local
granularity: NOTE 1's documentation standard is modeled as six LOCAL asserted
`code is` leaves combined by `defined as`. The CRE (run_decision v1) does NOT yet
evaluate `defined as` composition (asserting the leaves does not satisfy the
composite), so the canary case "documented nonunion (all six elements), no
exclusion -> Approve" FAILS today. That red is the intended proof-pending signal.
PROMOTE only after alphora/clinical-reasoning-language#126 lands and that canary
(and the drop-one-leaf adversarial cases) pass for the right reason.
The prior single-asserted-fold encoding (green, promoted) is preserved in git
history (commit on branch dme101-030-encoding).
=================================================================================

Encoding of HCSC Medical Policy DME101.030 (effective 2026-01-01), authored from
the refined source. Stage 1 (local-decision-support): every LEAF concept is a
LOCAL case-feature (`type is` + `code is` only); the only added depth is
`defined as` boolean composition over those local leaves — no `definition is`
predicates (count/temporal would compute over an external source), no value sets.
Dispositions are plain `activity` declarations.

Decision logic (from the source):
  Medically necessary (Approve) when ALL of:
    1. Documented nonunion of a fracture (per NOTE 1 — decomposed below); AND
    2. fracture is NOT of the skull or vertebrae; AND
    3. fracture is NOT tumor related.
  Not medically necessary (Deny) when criteria are not met — including a fresh
  fracture or delayed union (= absence of a documented nonunion -> `otherwise`)
  — OR when used with other noninvasive osteogenesis stimulators.

The three exclusions are ordered BEFORE the approval branch, so first-match
precedence makes any exclusion deny before approval is reached.

NOTE 1 DECOMPOSITION: the policy states HOW a nonunion must be documented. Each
sub-requirement is a LOCAL asserted boolean an upstream system determines and
asserts; the composite ANDs them. (Counts/intervals like "≥2 sets" and "≥90 days
apart" are asserted as booleans — `at-least-two-radiograph-sets` — NOT computed
via `definition is count …`, which would require an external source to count over
and is out of the local-source remit.)
*/

// ============ Exclusions (local asserted case-features) ============

// "used with other noninvasive osteogenesis stimulators" (Device is the
// stage-recommended type; the "concurrent use" relation is folded into the code).
concept "Concurrent Noninvasive Stimulator":
- type is Device.
- code is `concurrent-noninvasive-stimulator`.

concept "Skull Or Vertebral Fracture":
- type is Condition.
- code is `skull-or-vertebral-fracture`.

concept "Tumor Related Fracture":
- type is Condition.
- code is `tumor-related-fracture`.

// ============ Documented Nonunion — NOTE 1 decomposition (local asserted leaves) ============

concept "Nonunion Exists":
- type is Condition.
- code is `nonunion-exists`.

concept "At Least Two Radiograph Sets":
- type is Observation.
- code is `at-least-two-radiograph-sets`.

concept "Radiographs Obtained Prior To Treatment":
- type is Observation.
- code is `radiographs-prior-to-treatment`.

concept "Radiograph Sets At Least Ninety Days Apart":
- type is Observation.
- code is `radiograph-sets-at-least-ninety-days-apart`.

concept "Multiple Views Per Radiograph Set":
- type is Observation.
- code is `multiple-views-per-radiograph-set`.

concept "No Clinically Significant Interval Healing":
- type is Observation.
- code is `no-interval-healing-attested`.

// composite: satisfied iff all six NOTE-1 elements are asserted
concept "Documented Nonunion":
- defined as (
    "Nonunion Exists"
    sem-and "At Least Two Radiograph Sets"
    sem-and "Radiographs Obtained Prior To Treatment"
    sem-and "Radiograph Sets At Least Ninety Days Apart"
    sem-and "Multiple Views Per Radiograph Set"
    sem-and "No Clinically Significant Interval Healing"
  ).

// ============ Decision ============

decision "Ultrasonic Osteogenesis Stimulator Coverage Determination":
first:
- when "Concurrent Noninvasive Stimulator" then recommend activity "Deny".
- when "Skull Or Vertebral Fracture" then recommend activity "Deny".
- when "Tumor Related Fracture" then recommend activity "Deny".
- when "Documented Nonunion" then recommend activity "Approve".
- otherwise then recommend activity "Deny".

// ============ Activities (plain dispositions; shareable) ============

activity "Approve":
- request CPGServiceRequest.
- with `Authorize coverage of the ultrasonic osteogenesis stimulator as medically necessary.`.

activity "Deny":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `Ultrasonic osteogenesis stimulator is not medically necessary for this presentation.`.
